<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies eight issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies eight issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said it has qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--El Dorado, Kan., $2.887 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Kings Mountain, N.C., $7.02 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Washington Township, N.J., $6 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cortland, N.Y., $2.5 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Rotterdam CSD, N.Y., $2.37 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Philipsburg Area School District, Pa., $7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Virginia Housing Development, Va., $32.8 million revenue bonds and $25.8 million AMT revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
